-- DX EXPECTATION — §11.3.3, §3.1: there is no `max` in scope, so per
-- §11.3.3 the free lowercase head in the index of `m3` is implicitly
-- universalized (spec-mandated; the same universalization that makes
-- `useId : id Nat` legal).  The 2026-07-25 Nat/Fin revision does not add
-- a prelude `max` for Nat/Integer (§28.2.1 declares Max but exports no
-- term-level max; §28.2.3 requires no Max Nat), so the universalization
-- and the mismatch both still stand.  The DX gap is everything around
-- it: the resulting mismatch renders the universalized head as a bare
-- hole — "actual: P (_ 2 3) / expected: P 3" — with no mention of the
-- name `max`, no not-in-scope hint, and no note that the name was
-- universalized, while the identical TERM-level `max 2 3` gets a proper
-- E_NAME_UNRESOLVED with "did you mean 'map'?".  A typo in an index
-- function thus becomes a fresh binder and surfaces as a baffling
-- remote mismatch.  Expected: the mismatch renders the source name
-- (`P (max 2 3)`) and carries a help noting that `max` is not in scope
-- and was implicitly universalized (with the term-level did-you-mean
-- candidates).
-- Second rendering hazard, new with §28.2's inductive Nat: the expected
-- index 3 has a unary source normal form, and §34.3.2A forbids the unary
-- representation only at RUNTIME — nothing stops a renderer from
-- printing `P (Succ (Succ (Succ Zero)))`.  The payload assert pins the
-- numeral spelling `P 3`.
-- Cross-reference: prelude-min-max-unavailable.kp — §15.8.4 now REQUIRES
-- piecewise-linear min/max/clamp/abs solver reasoning while the prelude
-- still exports no min/max, so the solver can reason about an operation
-- users cannot name; the two files should be fixed together.
--! mode check
--! assertErrorCount 1
--! assertDiagnosticFamily error kappa.type.mismatch
--! assertDiagnosticMatch max
--! assertDiagnosticMatch not in scope
--! assertDiagnosticMatch universalized
--! assertDiagnosticPayload error kappa.type.mismatch /payload/expected P 3

module main

data P (n : Nat) : Type =
    MkP

m3 : P (max 2 3)
let m3 = MkP

m3AsLit : P 3
let m3AsLit = m3                --!! kappa.type.mismatch
-- STATUS(a0497523): FAIL — the single kappa.type.mismatch renders "actual: P (_ 2 3) / expected: P 3": the misspelled head became an anonymous universalized binder with no mention of 'max', no unresolved-name hint, and no universalization note (term-level `max 2 3` gets E_NAME_UNRESOLVED with "did you mean 'map'?")
-- (Recorded before the not-in-scope/universalized/payload asserts were
-- added 2026-07-25.)
